  "name": "spec parsing: malformed or unknown-key --spec JSON silently becomes details_md prose",
  "slug": "spec-parsing-malformed-or-unknown",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "spec parsing: malformed or unknown-key --spec JSON silently becomes details_md prose",
    "details_md": "parseSpecInput (src/tickets/spec.ts:61-83) falls back to details_md for anything that is not a clean known-keys JSON object. A typo key (e.g. description) or truncated JSON silently stores the whole JSON string as prose — this review's own first ticket hit it. Fix: when raw parses as a JSON object (or starts with {) but fails the known-keys/schema gate, error or at least warn loudly instead of silently degrading.",
    "acceptance": [
      "JSON-looking spec that fails the schema errors (USAGE_ERROR) or warns on stderr",
      "bare-markdown specs still land in details_md"
    ],
    "context": [
      "src/tickets/spec.ts:61"
    ],
